Why not: the planner asked again (1)

  UNUSABLE     Why does Seq Scan on orders not use an index?
               No index can serve the condition of Seq Scan on orders: even with sequential scans
               off, the planner still reads all of orders.
               Why: the condition applies date_trunc() to created_at, so an index on created_at
               cannot serve it
               → Rewrite the condition so that the column stands alone, such as a range of values
               instead of a function of the column, or index the expression itself.
               Planned again with enable_seqscan = off; estimated.
